From: MacGameFix
Subject: directmanipulation: a viewport can be set up, and stays without a contact

Nothing in Wine hands a touch or a precision touchpad's pointer to Direct Manipulation,
so no manipulation ever starts. The calls a program makes to set a viewport up returned
E_NOTIMPL all the same, and one that needs the set-up to succeed before it opens its
window never opens it: one built on GPUI stops with "failed to open window: initializing
Direct Manipulation: Not implemented (0x80004001)" (Swofty Launcher 1.10.35 on
NotProton's runner for CrossOver Preview 41303, Rosetta, 2026-11-23, once 0039 had given
it its fonts).

A viewport now keeps its rectangle, its status (building, enabled by Enable, disabled by
Disable and Abandon) and one event handler, which is held and never called;
IDirectManipulationManager::Activate and Deactivate, IDirectManipulationUpdateManager::
Update, and the viewport's SetContact and Stop succeed and do nothing. A program gets its
window; touchpad pinch and inertia do not happen, the wheel does.

--- a/dlls/directmanipulation/directmanipulation.c
+++ b/dlls/directmanipulation/directmanipulation.c
